## Golden rule: copy the exemplars

These files define the house style. Before writing new code of a given kind, read the matching
exemplar and mirror its structure exactly. Reading it also loads the detailed rules for that kind
of file, which are scoped to the paths below.

{{EXEMPLARS_TABLE}}

## Detailed rules

The craft rules live in `.claude/rules/`, each scoped to the files it governs. They load when you
open a matching file; read the relevant one before writing:

| File | Governs | Covers |
|---|---|---|
| `.claude/rules/page-objects.md` | `src/pages/**` | class contract, `isLoaded()`, method prefixes |
| `.claude/rules/components.md` | `src/components/**` | scoping, no base class, no `open()` |
| `.claude/rules/fixtures.md` | `src/fixtures/**` | injection, extending the base fixture, setup |
| `.claude/rules/specs.md` | `tests/**/*.spec.ts` | titles, `beforeEach`, DRY, data-driven loops |
| `.claude/rules/locators.md` | pages and components | the CSS ban, priority order, disambiguation |
| `.claude/rules/assertions.md` | pages, components, specs | web-first matchers, no manual waiting |
| `.claude/rules/isolation.md` | specs and fixtures | parallel safety, unique data |
| `.claude/rules/conventions.md` | all TypeScript | imports, naming, JSDoc, no hard-coding |

